**1. Travel time in the Earth frame**

\[
t_{\text{Earth}}=\frac{d}{v}= \frac{1.6\times10^{5}\ \text{ly}}{0.99999987\,c}
\approx 1.6\times10^{5}\ \text{yr}
\]

(The factor \(1/0.99999987\) changes the result by only \(\sim2\times10^{-5}\) yr, negligible.)

**2. Time dilation**

\[
\beta =0.99999987,\qquad 
\gamma =\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\beta^{2}}}
\]

\[
1-\beta^{2}=1-(0.99999987)^{2}\approx 2.6\times10^{-7}
\]

\[
\sqrt{1-\beta^{2}}\approx 5.1\times10^{-4}\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;
\gamma\approx\frac{1}{5.1\times10^{-4}}\approx 1.96\times10^{3}
\]

**3. Proper time experienced by the astronaut**

\[
\tau = \frac{t_{\text{Earth}}}{\gamma}
      \approx \frac{1.6\times10^{5}\ \text{yr}}{1.96\times10^{3}}
      \approx 8.3\times10^{1}\ \text{yr}
      \approx 83\ \text{years}
\]

The astronaut would age about 83 years during the journey. The closest answer choice is **81 years**.

**Answer: (A)**.

